From 5959749ff32935fd11bb5a29cd37d84663d134cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: x399 <x399@lab>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 16:53:41 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 04/14] zink: present into the window system's own memory with
 the GPU

A frame used to be read back from the GPU by the CPU and copied into the
window's bitmap.  With VK_EXT_external_memory_host the bitmap itself can
be handed to the GPU, so the copy that presents the frame writes the
application's memory directly and the CPU never touches the pixels; the
buffers the window system rotates through are imported once and kept.
Redrawing a window no longer goes through the GPU at all - the frame is
already in the bitmap, so it is simply shown again, which also keeps the
window's thread away from the context.

ZINK_NO_HOST_PRESENT falls back to the copy through the CPU.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_device_info.py  |   5 +
 src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_public.h        |   6 +
 src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_screen.c        | 155 ++++++++++++++++++
 src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_screen.h        |  12 ++
 .../targets/haiku-zink/GalliumContext.cpp     |  10 +-
 5 files changed, 183 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

